  "text": "Recipe: Amaranth Greens & Chana Dal Vada\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: split chickpeas (chana dal), amaranth greens, onions, green chili, cilantro, cumin seeds, fennel seeds, red pepper flakes, grated ginger, ground flaxseed, turmeric powder, curry leaves, Salt\nCooking methods: blend, no-cook, bake\nInstructions: (1) GROUND CHANA DAL: Soak chana dal (split chickpeas) for 1-2 hours. Then grind them in a blender (without adding any water) into a coarse texture.\n(2) GREENS & MASALA: Mix thinly diced onions, green chilies, cilantro and amaranth greens with our hands, squeezing hard. Add cumin seeds, ground flaxseed, fennel seeds, red pepper flakes & grated ginger. Mix well. Add salt to taste.\n(3) VADAS: Combine Ground Chana Dal (from Step 1) with the Greens & Masala mixture (from Step 2). Mix well. Make small balls. Place them on a baking tray lined with parchment paper. Press them flat.\n(4) BAKE: Preheat the oven at 400 F. Place the baking tray with vadas in the oven. Bake for 10-15 minutes (until Vadas turn golden brown). Check in between to make sure that they don't burn.\n(5) SERVE: With homemade tomato sauce. They are nice and crunchy!",
